              <i class="bi bi-chat-square-text"></i>
            </div>
            <h3 class="zin-h3">Generic output is not a prompting problem.</h3>
            <p class="zin-body-sm mb-0">
              It is an input problem. A vague brief produces something anyone could have written, which means no one wrote it.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="col-md-4">
        <div class="card h-100">
          <div class="card-body">
            <div class="d-inline-flex align-items-center justify-content-center fs-2 mb-3 p-2 rounded-3" style="background-color: #fff3e0; color: #fd7e15;">
              <i class="bi bi-fingerprint"></i>
            </div>
            <h3 class="zin-h3">AI sounds like you when you feed it your thinking.</h3>
            <p class="zin-body-sm mb-0">
              That is Zin's job. Your stories, your observations, your hard-won lessons, captured over time and kept ready. When you sit down to create, the material is already there, and it is already yours.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="col-md-4">
        <div class="card h-100">
          <div class="card-body">
            <div class="d-inline-flex align-items-center justify-content-center fs-2 mb-3 p-2 rounded-3" style="background-color: #fff3e0; color: #fd7e15;">
              <i class="bi bi-box-arrow-up-right"></i>
            </div>
            <h3 class="zin-h3">There is no AI inside Zin.</h3>
            <p class="zin-body-sm mb-0">
              That is deliberate. Every thought in your library is one you actually had. When you want AI to work with your thinking, you choose the thoughts, and Zin assembles them into a prompt for the tool you already use.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

